Learnings
  ✓ Implemented deterministic default multi-run reconciliation planning with optional runIds filters, sorted unique candidate run IDs, exact settled-and-closed preimages, and fresh bounded atomic apply. Targeted reconciliation tests passed (3/3); npx tsc --noEmit passed. Tests evidence live-shaped multi-run discovery, deterministic digest, filtering, stale-lineage rejection, idempotence, no deletion, and no synthetic end.
  ⚠ Implemented a verified apply-time approval claim binding canonical request digest, canonical decision digest, request ID, subject digest, decision timestamp, and validated live authority reference. Missing authorization returns a fail-closed HOLD marker without applying reconciliation; self approval, stale authorization, exact request/decision tampering, denied decisions, and a different reconciliation batch are rejected. Verified with `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vitest run tests/core/provider-execution-observation-reconciliation-approval.test.ts` (3 passing tests).
  ✓ Bound the verified approval claim into content-addressed reconciliation receipts. Fresh reads now preserve historical before/after evidence while requiring the current schema and every exact candidate row to remain retired, so unrelated legitimate append/retire activity remains valid. Verified with npx tsc --noEmit and npx vitest run tests/core/provider-execution-observation-reconciliation-receipt-store.test.ts (5 tests passed).

